  "term": "pavor",
  "definition": "Pavor refers to a state of terror or alarm, especially in the historical expression pavor nocturnus, meaning night-terrors in children. In this condition, a child suddenly wakes in fright during sleep, behaves as if seeing imaginary dangers, and usually has no memory of the episode the next day.",
